-- title:
--   Open stabilisers of places under constant-field base change
-- statement:
--   Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$, i.e. a subfield of the field of Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ containing $\mathbb{Q}$, and assume $F_0$ is a function field of one variable over $\mathbb{Q}$ in the sense that there is an element $x$ of $F_0$ transcendental over $\mathbb{Q}$ for which $F_0$ is finite-dimensional over the subfield $\mathbb{Q}(x)$ generated by $x$ inside $F_0$. Write $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}F_0$ for `laurentBaseChange (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) F₀`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the image of $F_0$ under the coefficientwise extension of $\mathbb{Q} \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ on Laurent series. Let $v$ be a place of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}F_0$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, that is, a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}F_0$ which contains the image of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, is not the whole field, and is a principal ideal ring. Then there exists an intermediate field $L_0$ of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Q}$, such that for every $\sigma \in \mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ fixing $L_0$ pointwise, the semilinear automorphism [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois F₀ σ`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) — the pair consisting of the coefficientwise action of $\sigma$ on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}F_0$ together with $\sigma$ itself on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ — carries $v$ to $v$.
--
--   This is the statement that the stabiliser of a place of a constant-field base change is open in the Krull topology, so that each geometric point of the curve with function field $F_0$ is defined over a number field; classically this belongs to the theory of constant field extensions of algebraic function fields. It is used in the construction of an inertia-stable degree-zero divisor class on the modular curve, via [`ModularCurve.exists_inertiaStable_degZero_pic0Mk_eq_xH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_inertiaStable_degZero_pic0Mk_eq_xH).
